# ProfileCard Component Rules
<!-- This is a comment. Students can read this. Cursor will ignore it semantically. -->

## Product Overview
<!-- 2–3 sentences describing the purpose and function of the ProfileCard component. -->
ProfileCard displays a user's identity and role in a compact, scannable format. It surfaces the avatar, display name, title, and bio, plus primary actions (Follow and Message) so viewers can connect at a glance. Use it anywhere a person summary is needed—team directories, author bios, or social previews.


## Props
- `name` (string) – User's display name
- `title` (string) – Role or subtitle (e.g., "Designer & Engineer")
- `bio` (string) – Short description
- `avatarUrl` (optional string) – Image URL; fallback to blank circle when absent


## Typography
Use intentional, hierarchy-driven typography:
<!-- Try changing one of the following text properties (Name, Title, or Bio). For context...
   - text-* (-2xl, -3xl, -sm, -medium, etc) define the text size.
   - font-* (-medium, -semibold, -normal, etc) define the font weight. 
   - text-*color*-### defines the text color and opacity. 
   - see typography documentation here -> https://v3.tailwindcss.com/docs/font-size -->
- **Name**: `text-2xl`, `font-bold`, `tracking-tight`, `text-white`
- **Title**: `text-sm`, `font-medium`, `text-zinc-400`
- **Bio**: `text-sm`, `leading-relaxed`, `text-zinc-300`

Avoid `font-black` and `font-light` extremes unless explicitly required for the design system.


## Layout & Spacing
<!-- Students should not edit. -->
- Card: `max-w-md`, `rounded-2xl`, `p-6`
- Avatar: `h-14 w-14`, `rounded-full`
- Gap between avatar and content: `gap-4`
- Bio margin-top: `mt-5`
- Buttons: `mt-6`, `gap-2`


## Buttons
<!-- Students should not edit. -->
- Primary (Follow): filled, high contrast
- Secondary (Message): bordered, lower emphasis
- Both: `rounded-lg`, `px-3 py-2`, `text-sm`

